  "scope": "Repair the existing hypercurve_ui restricted-fragment output failures and retain exact in-memory sources behind editable previews. No kernel or CI Rust changes; no property, target, or crate future-work completion claim.",
  "contract": [
    "If exact boundary paths exist but their geometry cannot supply editable primitives, use the existing family-preserving finite curve projection for the preview.",
    "Keep the original CurveRegion2 and each available CurvePath2. Compare editor snapshots before source reuse. Direct control, closure, loop-role, or source replacement invalidates reuse.",
    "Display segmentation carries the same exact source. A projected boundary with no exact path returns an error if extracted for topology. Native line/arc adapters reject retained higher-order paths instead of substituting display chords.",
    "The existing finite JSON/URL authoring format remains a documented lossy boundary. Exact sources are serde-skipped in-memory state. Actual edits author new geometry."
  ],
